# Docs: example section titles

Under `## Common examples`, each `###` heading names the **pattern or use case** the section teaches. The live demo may show a concrete product scene (price filter, equalizer, teammate search) — that scene belongs in preview copy and prose, **not** in the heading.

## Do

- Title the capability or compose pattern: dual thumbs, grouped options, external label row, as a link, loading
- Keep headings short and scannable (same voice as Button: Variants, Addons, Pill)
- Let demo labels, `label` props, and the lead sentence under the heading carry the product story

## Do not

- Name the heading after incidental demo UI (Price range, Billing plans, Teammate search, Graphic equalizer)
- Restate the component name alone (`### Slider`) or dump prop inventories into the title
- Mirror Ask-your-agent tab labels into `###` headings — prompts stay consumer intents; example titles stay patterns

## Examples

| Avoid (demo UI) | Prefer (pattern / use case) |
| --- | --- |
| Price range | Dual thumbs |
| Control saturation | Controlled preview |
| Linked equalizer | Linked vertical bands |
| Teammate search | Filterable options |
| Free-form category | Free-form value |
| Timezone groups | Grouped options |
| Billing plans | Labeled group |
| Email alerts group | Labeled group |
| Billing details section | Labeled section |
| Delivery RadioGroup | Nested RadioGroup |
| Plan cards with group error | Group error |
| Form footer boolean | Standalone checkbox |

## Out of scope

- Ask-your-agent `text tab="…"` labels — those stay plain-language consumer intents (see `.cursor/rules/02-docs-consumer-voice.mdc`)
- Live demo product copy inside `src/components/demos/**`
